// std/currency.dag -- ISO 4217 currency identity + minor-unit authority.
//
// `CurrencyCode` is the ISO 4217 *alphabetic code* enum -- the stable
// identity of a currency. The richer per-currency data (minor-unit
// exponent, numeric code, display name) is a cited projection keyed by
// the code, not structure the tag dissolves into. This is the same layering
// as the OS distribution identity enum at `dsl/std/os/types.dag`
// ("enum tag is stable id; catalog row is cited authority").
//
// Authority anchors (cited by rule-text quote; bare line-number cites prohibited):
//   - spec-primitive disposition: a type modeling a spec primitive carries a
//     🔴/🟡/🟢 disposition and names its cited external authority. ISO 4217 is
//     that authority here.
//   - coproduct decomposition (DESIGN.md §2 decompress→map→reduce):
//     "🟢 terminal -- the variants are irreducible distinctions at the
//     user-input boundary (literals, keywords, source locations); no richer
//     structure can be named."
//   - construction over ratchets: "Don't build ... ahead of
//     consumer demand." -> variants are enrolled per consumer demand, not
//     pre-populated to the full ISO 4217 register.
//
// External authority (spec primitive):
//   ISO 4217:2015 "Codes for the representation of currencies" -- the
//   alphabetic code register and per-currency minor-unit (exponent) table.
//   The *domain* is closed against ISO 4217 (no ad-hoc currencies); the
//   enrolled *variants* grow as consumers denominate in them.

module std.currency

import std.types { Int }

// --- CurrencyCode: ISO 4217 alphabetic code (stable currency identity) ----
//
// DECOMPOSITION CHECKPOINT (DESIGN.md §2): 🟢 TERMINAL (spec primitive)
// Each variant is an ISO 4217 alphabetic code -- an irreducible identity at
// the financial-spec boundary. Dissolution patterns considered and rejected
// (recorded for PR review):
//   - "dissolve into a CurrencyCatalogRow record (numeric code, name,
//     minor-unit exponent, ...)": rejected -- the row is data *keyed by*
//     the code, not richer structure the tag reduces to. The code is the
//     key; the row is a projection. Same disposition as the OS distribution
//     identity enum (`std/os/types.dag`). The only currently-demanded
//     projection is the minor-unit exponent (`currency_minor_unit_exponent`
//     below); a full catalog row is deferred until a consumer needs it
//     (construction over ratchets — no carrier ahead of consumer demand).
//
// CLOSED DOMAIN / EXTENSION RULE: the domain is closed against ISO 4217 --
// no ad-hoc currencies. Variants are enrolled per consumer demand only.
// Adding a code requires (a) a real consumer denominating in it and
// (b) its ISO 4217 minor-unit exponent in `currency_minor_unit_exponent`
// (construction over ratchets — no variant ahead of consumer demand).
// Eur is the live compute-supply consumer (Hetzner cost quotes); Usd is the
// ISO 4217 reference numeraire, exercised by the money-carrier claim-run.
type CurrencyCode =
    Eur     // ISO 4217 "EUR" -- euro (minor unit: cent, 10^-2)
  | Usd     // ISO 4217 "USD" -- US dollar (minor unit: cent, 10^-2)

// --- currency_minor_unit_exponent: ISO 4217 minor-unit authority ----------
//
// Structural projection from a `CurrencyCode` to its ISO 4217 minor-unit
// exponent: the number of decimal places between the major unit (e.g. euro)
// and the minor unit (e.g. cent). This is the single cited authority any
// consumer binds against rather than re-encoding the per-currency table at
// the call site (single-source-of-truth, cf. `scale_exponent` in
// `std/measure.dag`).
//
// The exponent is NON-NEGATIVE (minor units subdivide the major unit), so
// EUR/USD = 2 (cents), and a zero-minor-unit currency (e.g. JPY) would be 0.
// The value is the count of minor-unit decimal places, NOT an SI `Scale`:
// ISO minor units (10^-2 cents) are not an SI decimal scale value (no
// `Centi` in `Scale`), so currency minor-unit semantics live here, never
// forced onto the dimensional `Scale` axis.
//
// Total over all enrolled `CurrencyCode` inhabitants.
fn currency_minor_unit_exponent(c: CurrencyCode) -> Int {
  match c {
    Eur => 2
    Usd => 2
  }
}
